  accTitle: The same context window, today and with ltms
  accDescr: Two context windows of the same size. Today, memory is kept in the window: beside instructions and notes sit memory loaded in (wiki pages, earlier work, as much as fits) and, after a compaction, a summary of the earlier work, so little room is left for the work; the session files on your disk are hard to read back. With ltms, memory is kept on disk and read back when needed, even after a compaction: the window holds instructions, notes and the skill, a small outline, and one line read by its address; the rest of the window is for the work, which Claude Code still compacts to a summary when the window fills.
